Test ID: TC10 (bounded local protocol-resilience subcheck)
Date: 2026-11-27
Target: 127.0.0.1:9000; listener was confirmed loopback-only.
Traffic: Anonymous PING requests only; no login, account data, or credentials.

Observed:
- 50 concurrent TCP clients each received a valid framed response: PASS.
- A frame sent in fragments with a 1-second pause was accepted: PASS.
- A peer closing after a partial header did not prevent a subsequent PING: PASS.
- Malformed JSON was rejected without a success response: PASS.
- An advertised body length of 65,537 bytes was rejected: PASS.

Limitations:
- This was not a sustained authenticated/gameplay load test and did not measure throughput or latency.
- Clumsy impairment was not applied.
- TC10 remains PARTIAL; these loopback checks do not establish production capacity.

Redaction: No credentials, account identifiers, OTPs, tokens, or public endpoints were used or recorded.
